# Accessible visual output

- The user cannot view rendered Codex Canvas files; a `.canvas.tsx` file appears only as source code to them.
- Do not use `.canvas.tsx` as the only user-facing visual or analytical deliverable.
- For static architecture diagrams, roadmaps, flows, and graphs, prefer inline Mermaid that renders in the conversation.
- When richer graphics are needed, provide an inline-visible image or another format the user can directly open.
- If a Canvas is required by higher-level instructions, also provide the complete result in an accessible inline format.
